---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config";
---
<Base title="Contact" description="Contact SolTechnology about licences, support and partnerships.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Contact</h1>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line p-6">
        <h2 class="font-semibold">Licences &amp; support</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-[15px]">Licence quotes, purchase orders, bank transfers, and questions from licence holders (please add your licence number).</p>
        <a class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium text-deep underline" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line p-6">
        <h2 class="font-semibold">Bugs &amp; questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted text-[15px]">Anything about how the libraries work: GitHub issues, so the answer helps others too.</p>
        <a class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium text-deep underline" href="https://github.com/AdrianStrugala/AvroConvert/issues">AvroConvert issues</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-mist p-6 text-[15px]">
      <h2 class="font-semibold">Orders, invoices and refunds</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-ink/80">Purchases are processed by Polar Software, Inc., our reseller and Merchant of Record, which issues the invoice. Your order e-mail from Polar links to a customer portal where you can download the invoice, add a company name or VAT number, or cancel the renewal; for refund requests you can also contact Polar at <a class="underline" href="mailto:support@polar.sh">support@polar.sh</a>. Purchase orders and bank transfers are handled directly by us – write to <a class="underline" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-10 text-xs text-muted">{site.legalName} · {site.legalAddress} · {site.legalTaxId}</p>
  </section>
</Base>
